# Content board

Nathan’s handoff is **Save in the F5 in-game editor, then close the game.** That writes `data/content-board.json` and `data/catalog.json`. Closing the game is enough. He does not need to say “check the board,” and it does not matter what the next message is about.

The HTML board (`design/content-board.html`) is the same SoT if he used Zen instead.

## Every message in this repo

Read `data/content-board.json` (HTML only if the JSON is missing). Then:

1. **Player-facing Save (ability, explainer, name, numbers, tier)** — already on disk. Use that text. Do not make him re-dictate it. If `author_lock` is set (see `author-lock.mdc` / `data/author-locks.json`), do not rewrite those fields at all unless this chat clearly overrides, and stop to ask first.
2. **Behavior Save (Flow, Notes, Ops JSON, ATK/HP formulas)** — if it does not match live code in `scripts/main.gd` (and related scripts), that card is a ship queue. If Flow/Notes already settle the edges, implement. If the change is new or ambiguous, **Paper Fight first** (`design/paper-fight/RUBRIC.md`) — do not invent Hornet/Queen/block/targeting. In-game Save flips status to `todo` when those fields change.
3. Skip `hold` and `retired` unless he named them.
4. **Your notes for Cursor** (`review_note`) win. Read every non-empty one. If that note disagrees with ability, explainer, flow, notes, ops, or an older design doc, build the note. Do not Paper Fight to keep the older sentence. Do not ask him to retype it. If the note states new player-facing words, write those words — the saved note is the override. Leave locked fields the note does not mention alone.
   When the note obviously replaces a sentence, a number, or a formula, delete the old text everywhere he can still read it: the board, the catalog, the explainer, the call name, the shift line, flow, notes, ops, and any hardcoded fallback or editor default. Write the new text in that place. He should not see the previous version next to the new one. If you are not sure a field is the leftover, ask before deleting it.
5. If Ability, Flow, and Notes disagree and **Your notes for Cursor** is empty, Paper Fight — do not guess.
6. After shipping code, set those cards to `live` on the board and in catalog/runtime. Stamp each shipped card in `data/recent-edits.json` (`recent_edits.gd` `touch`, or `{ "monster:id" / "item:id": unix }`) so **Play Latest** picks them up.

If nothing needs a code change, do not mention this check.

## Do not

- Do not treat leftover `todo` from the old HTML board as “finish the whole roster.” Cards already in the dungeon, and cards he previously told you not to build, stay as they are unless **this Save** (or a named request) changed them.
- Do not wait for the phrases **check for item updates** / **check the board** — those still mean the same pass, but they are not required.
